1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,068
Voices.

2
00:00:01,298 --> 00:00:03,072
Pictures, swinging on the walls.

3
00:00:03,302 --> 00:00:05,337
That's what people have reported inside

4
00:00:05,347 --> 00:00:07,359
Tippecanoe Place, in South Bend.

5
00:00:07,909 --> 00:00:10,434
Wagon maker Clem Studebaker had this

6
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:11,926
40-room stone mansion built.

7
00:00:12,156 --> 00:00:14,065
It was finished in 1889.

8
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:16,507
That same year, fire tore through it.

9
00:00:16,738 --> 00:00:17,692
The roof burned.

10
00:00:17,922 --> 00:00:19,553
Much of the inside was gutted.

11
00:00:19,783 --> 00:00:21,301
But the stone walls survived.

12
00:00:21,851 --> 00:00:23,383
It was restored within a year.

13
00:00:23,613 --> 00:00:25,228
Clem died in 1901.

14
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:28,046
In World War 2, the house was a Red Cross

15
00:00:28,056 --> 00:00:28,660
headquarters.

16
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:30,976
Later, it was a school for disabled

17
00:00:30,986 --> 00:00:31,398
children.

18
00:00:31,848 --> 00:00:34,067
In 1980, it became a restaurant.

19
00:00:34,717 --> 00:00:37,093
Legend says some of the Studebakers never

20
00:00:37,103 --> 00:00:37,376
left.

21
00:00:38,226 --> 00:00:40,971
The restaurant closed in January 2026.

22
00:00:41,201 --> 00:00:42,623
Please view it from the road.

23
00:00:43,173 --> 00:00:45,216
Comment your town, and it could be next.

